From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:16:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: apple: describe the T8011 PDM controller

The A10X PDM controller uses the same register layout with different SmartIO DMA configuration. Give it a separate compatible to select the DMA data.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,t8010-pdm.yaml       | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,t8010-pdm.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,t8010-pdm.yaml
index 4a311d690..93928c249 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,t8010-pdm.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,t8010-pdm.yaml
@@ -4,14 +4,15 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/sound/apple,t8010-pdm.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Apple T8010 PDM microphone controller
+title: Apple T8010 and T8011 PDM microphone controller
 
 maintainers:
   - Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
 
 description:
   The PDM microphone controller of the Apple A10 records the built-in
-  PDM microphones. Each microphone has a HiFi decimator that filters its
+  PDM microphones. T8011 uses a different SmartIO FIFO and trigger pair.
+  Each microphone has a HiFi decimator that filters its
   bit stream down to PCM; the controller hands the samples to SmartIO
   DMA. The PDM clock comes from the Always-On Processor's audio service.
 
@@ -20,7 +21,9 @@ allOf:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: apple,t8010-pdm
+    enum:
+      - apple,t8010-pdm
+      - apple,t8011-pdm
 
   reg:
     minItems: 2
